<h3>Emerging directions (mid-2026)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Self-distillation without external teachers</strong> — SSB (2512.05105), ROSD (2605.28014), SSOPD (2605.17497): single-model distillation using different contexts or verified rollouts. <strong>SDPO</strong> (2601.20802) is architecturally distinct: rather than contrasting a current vs. past model, the student conditions on <em>textual feedback about its own errors</em> (e.g., runtime error messages, judge critiques) to generate corrective token-level supervision — the model distills its own feedback-conditioned self back into the unconditioned policy, achieving 3× better sample efficiency than GRPO on scientific reasoning and LiveCodeBench</li>
  <li><strong>Offline OPD — removing the live-teacher requirement</strong> — <strong>Lightning OPD</strong> (2604.13010) precomputes teacher log-probabilities over SFT rollouts once, then reuses them throughout training, achieving <strong>4× training efficiency</strong> over standard OPD. Its key theoretical finding is "teacher consistency": the SFT teacher and OPD teacher <em>must be the same model</em> — mixing them introduces gradient bias that degrades performance even when the OPD teacher is stronger. This retroactively explains failures that practitioners have likely seen empirically. Qwen3-8B trained with Lightning OPD reaches 69.9% AIME 2024 on a single 8×H100 node in 30 GPU hours</li>
  <li><strong>Stabilisation under long horizons</strong> — f-OPD (2605.17862) addresses sample staleness in async OPD; Veto/Stable-OPD (2601.07155) handles pathological FKL/RKL gradients</li>
  <li><strong>RL + OPD jointly</strong> — dGRPO (2605.12227), SDAR (2605.15155), Search-E1 (2605.22511): combine sparse RL rewards with dense distillation supervision. <strong>CoDistill-GRPO</strong> (2605.08873) inverts the usual teacher-fixed assumption: a large and small model co-train from the start — the small model's rollouts train the large model (via importance reweighting), while the large model's output distribution provides an OPD reward to the small model, yielding 18% faster large-model training by offloading rollout generation</li>
  <li><strong>Multimodal extension</strong> — vision-OPD (2605.21924) adds visual advantage weighting; VLA-OPD (2603.26666) extends to robot action models</li>
  <li><strong>Theoretical grounding</strong> — "Post-Training is About States, Not Tokens" (2605.22731) unifies SFT, RL, and OPD through a state-distribution lens, suggesting on-policy state coverage is as important as the loss form</li>
</ul>
</section>

